This crate (`symphonia-codec-twinvq`) is a from-scratch, pure-Rust NTT TwinVQ (VQF) decoder. It is
licensed under the Mozilla Public License, v. 2.0, like the rest of Project Symphonia.

TwinVQ has no public specification. The bitstream layout, the mode table, the dequantization, the
bark envelope, the periodic peak component (PPC), the LSP decoding and spectral envelope
evaluation, the inverse MDCT windowing and the output stage follow FFmpeg's
`libavcodec/twinvq.c`, `libavcodec/twinvqdec.c` and `libavcodec/twinvq.h`. The codebooks, bark band
tables, LSP tables and permutation tables in `src/tables.rs` (extracted programmatically) are
those of `libavcodec/twinvq_data.h` and `libavcodec/metasound_twinvq_data.h`. These files are
distributed under the GNU Lesser General Public License, version 2.1 or later.

